description:
This new dissector adds support for the MCData protocol as defined by 3GPP TS 24.282.

The most common ON-NETWORK use cases are supported and missing functionality is marked in the "TODO:" section of the initial comment. 
I was told by AI that such missing functionality is no obstacle for this to be merged and I hope that this is really the case. I currently do not have the time and appropriate test data to implement the missing functionality.

I'm unsure about the policy here when it comes to testing such a dissector, which only gets called as MIME part dissector. This is the reason why I marked the merge request as "draft". Please see the last lines of the code:

```
    // The following line is used for testing 3GPP MCData over UDP only, which does not exist in the standard
    // Question to the reviewers: What is the policy here? Shall this be removed?
    // The real protocol stack e.g. UDP/SIP/MIME body/ application/vnd.3gpp.mcdata-payload or application/vnd.3gpp.mcdata-signalling is too complicated
    dissector_add_uint_with_preference("udp.port", 7777, mcdata_handle);
```

